+## fastq-running-tasks
+
+The API provides runningTasks(): T[] to callback and promise queues, returning a fresh shallow snapshot of task values whose worker has started and has not called its completion callback (or settled its worker promise). Preserve start order within the snapshot and duplicates, including undefined values. At entry to a task completion callback its value must already be absent from runningTasks. Queued or paused work is excluded until actually started. Cover direct push/unshift, promotion from the queue, resume and concurrency changes. Task object pooling must not corrupt a previously returned snapshot or retain completed values. Keep running(), getQueue(), error/callback receivers, results, rejection, drain and existing scheduling behavior unchanged.
